@copyleft MC Marinica, R Alexander

Sources of Insert_Sias. The full documentation is in ../doc; the build is
described in ../doc/install.md.


Compilation
-----------

With CMake, from the root of the repository (gfortran is taken first, then ifx;
add -DCMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER=ifx to choose):

cmake -B build ; cmake --build build

Or with the makefiles of this directory:

Makefile_gfortran - Makefile for gfortran
Makefile_ifx      - Makefile for the Intel compiler (set FC = ifort for the
                    classic one)
Makefile.common   - the rules, included by the two files above

cp Makefile_gfortran Makefile ; make

Either way the executables are written to bin:

cube.x            builds the perfect bcc or fcc reference crystal
put_vct.x         inserts the defects
pre_put_vct.x     generates the list of sites of a dislocation loop
read_write_n00.x  translates a list of sites
cube_shell.x      reference crystal with an inner block listed first

Most work needs only cube.x and put_vct.x, plus pre_put_vct.x for loops.


Layout
------

programs/   one source file per executable, named after it
lib/        the routines of put_vct.x
bin/        the executables
Modules/    module files of the makefile build
obj/        object files of the makefile build (created by make)


programs/
---------

put_vct.f90         the main program of put_vct.x. It reads the input, finds
                    the atoms of the listed sites and calls the routines of
                    lib/ that build each type of defect. The lattice
                    parameter and the dumbbell lengths are set at its top.
cube.f              cube.x
cube_shell.f90      cube_shell.x
pre_put_vct.f90     pre_put_vct.x, self-contained, with its own parameters
read_write_n00.f90  read_write_n00.x


lib/
----

Reading and sites

input.f90           reads the defect type, formd.str and the list of sites
sites.f90           integer coordinates of the atoms, in units of a0/2, and
                    search of the atoms that sit on the listed sites

Defects

point_defects.f90   dumbbells, Gao di-interstitials, vacancies: geometry
                    and output files
migration.f90       the two states of a dumbbell jump
clusters.f90        C15 and icosahedral clusters: atoms removed, atoms
                    inserted, output files
kazuto_style.f90    the rotated cut of defect type 67

Output

lammps_output.f90   module lammps_output: LAMMPS data files

Modules of data

module_defect_types.f90   the defect types as named constants
                          (DEFECT_VACANCY, DEFECT_C15, ...) and the functions
                          that group them (defect_is_cluster, ...). The
                          sources test the type with these names, never with
                          its number.
module_octahedre.f90      geometry of the C15 unit (module octahedre) and
                          of the icosahedral unit (module icosaedre)
module_111_smooth.f90     row relaxation of defect types 21 and 221
module_100_smooth.f90     row relaxation of defect type 31
module_migration_sia.f90  data of the dumbbell jumps
module_pbc.f90            cell matrix and its inverse

Mathematics

math.f90            module math: 3x3 determinant and inverse, vector product
rotations.f90       rotation of a vector
indexx.f90          index sort
lapack.f            LAPACK routines, for the matrix inverse of math.f90

Every file starts with a comment that lists its routines.
